  "2026-11-01T04:53:36.301Z",codex-agent,"Initial limited triage: PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRpr is valid. The old current_packed_acceptance objects named runtime a450cdb and archive 5b632744; both complete objects are regenerated from the already successful fresh capture, naming runtime fc3d8fc and archive 23c873d7343083b1fe7013d5d98cbc08957e2b6f0bd47015c7d8ca7ac5d7ddd9, with measured file counts and six fresh/two replay passes. The shipped public receipt and its native roots were certified unchanged by both retained-fixture replays. No runtime code changed for this receipt correction. The remaining batch requires its own current-code triage. No external thread replies or resolutions were sent."
  "2026-11-01T04:53:46.699Z",codex-agent,"PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqU is factually incorrect on the current implementation. executeReservedProcessJob reads a certified ProcessSnapshot after publishing running, then compares it with the published running job and raises superseded/exit 4 with Process advanced before launch before any trainer launcher is called. The test injects after a native historical get, not after readProcessSnapshot has certified the final history head. Its fixed control passes and explicitly requires that pre-launch message plus unchanged peer document/history. Removing that pre-launch comparison fails the recorded before-launch sensitivity probe. The workspace transaction lease is not being treated as exclusion against ordinary writers. This rebuttal is recorded only here; external resolution belongs to the orchestrator."
  "2026-11-01T04:55:42.094Z",codex-agent,"Correction to the preceding explanation of PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqU: readProcessSnapshot captures a history coordinate and reads that version; it does NOT certify a final history head. The selected second historical get after the committed hook is the post-publication reread in commitProcessTransition. The executor subsequently rereads before comparing with the published running job, so this specific injected test case does hit the pre-launch refusal, as its required message and sensitivity proof show. A write after the final executor snapshot is a different window and remains part of the separate review triage. The earlier statement about final-head certification in the snapshot helper was incorrect; this append-only correction narrows the rebuttal to the test scenario actually proved."
  "2026-11-01T07:31:25.077Z",codex-agent,"Current-head inventory is 27 unresolved Cubic threads: four P1, eighteen P2, five P3. Claimed this batch separately from earlier coverage work. Plan: reproduce ownership and path races, preserve released read compatibility and forward-only native writes, then focused behavioral and revert checks, unchanged quality gates, one batched push. Three alleged failing-test cases pass unchanged: authoritative status reads (including native and typed failures), prospective chronology preflight, and publication-to-read races; exact results will be included with the final classifications."
  "2026-11-01T07:42:59.819Z",codex-agent,"Blocking reproduction: PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRp3 is valid. A real fs/promises mkdir interleaving swaps locks after statePath validation; acquireStateLock then succeeds and creates confined.lock in the outside tripwire. The same raw SDK-root delegation is present in acquireStateLease and commitStateTransaction. Pinned SDK 2026.10.27 and inspected latest 2026.11.1 expose only pathname-based lock APIs; SDK cleanup creates a replaceable directory and later writes owner.json by pathname. Rechecking once or pinning only the parent cannot certify the whole operation. Tracked unresolved dependency as pm-rl-confined-sdk-locks with explicit no-follow, interoperability, must-refuse and must-allow criteria. This P1 remains blocking; it is not marked fixed or rejected."
  "2026-11-01T07:47:42.386Z",codex-agent,"Current triage table (provisional gate and sensitivity receipts are completed by later append-only comments). 23 implemented fixes, 3 factual rebuttals, 1 unresolved blocking P1. The dependency row is explicitly unfinished, not an approved P1 deferral.\n\n| Thread | Priority | Classification | Change or reason | Revert proof / evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRpu | P1 | fixed | Missing config after ownership is typed process_job_drift; prelaunch absence still succeeds. | R1: removing post-observation refusal makes missing-after-observation succeed. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRp2 | P1 | fixed | Guard nested history ids on run and runTyped before delegation, preserving SDK aliases. | R2: removing the guard returns native history errors instead of rl_identifier_invalid/2. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRp3 | P1 | UNRESOLVED: pm-rl-confined-sdk-locks | Real parent-swap reproduction writes confined.lock outside state. SDK has no descriptor-relative primitive; no atomic confinement claim or superficial recheck shipped. | Reproduction succeeds on current code; blocking dependency, no fix or passing regression claimed. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRp4 | P1 | fixed | Retain original child handle when runner identity was not durably published, including identity-read and runner-write failures; bounded retry uses that exact handle. | R7: restoring detach loses retained_child_handle in identity case; runner-specific proof pending. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRp6 | P2 | fixed | Each cycle uses the prior promoted candidate and its current native version. Compact card refs still match complete native receipt manifests. | R8: restoring seed incumbent fails rl-seed versus rl-candidate before the corruption matrix. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRp9 | P2 | not valid | Authoritative status uses getTypedItem/direct SDK reads, not the claimed normalized reader; unchanged native and typed status cases pass. index.ts:3602,4778. | Unchanged focused reproduction passes both backend_unavailable and native unavailable cases. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRp_ | P2 | fixed | Restore exact one-promotion assertion together with typed budget_exceeded. | Focused padded-approval budget test passes; assertion restoration is the test fix. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqA | P2 | fixed | Keep strict write refusals and restore legacy padded-parent normalization and environment contamination checks. | Parser and padded-environment tests pass with both read and write contracts. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqD | P2 | fixed | Resolve checkpoint boundary outside missing-byte catch. Missing artifact and valid persisted bytes retain their outcomes. | R3: moving path validation back into catch yields lm_checkpoint_artifact_missing instead of boundary/2. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqE | P2 | fixed | Generated probe branches without process.exit, allowing pipe output to drain naturally. | Packed compatibility and delayed-output sensitivity pending final archive. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqG | P2 | fixed | Shared PATH helper looks up the native birth tool directly and copies executables on Windows; no POSIX-shell dependency. | Native restricted-PATH test passes; platform sensitivity pending. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqK | P2 | not valid | The actual SDK harness rethrows errors carrying numeric exitCode. Expected-code cases require that typed exception; handled:false is reserved for untyped released assertions. | Unchanged prospective chronology test passes both fixed/sequential modes and both output modes. SDK testing.d.ts:662-663 documents propagation. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqN | P2 | fixed | Parse TOON and deep-compare complete export and replay envelopes with same-command JSON before asserting json_and_toon. | Final packed acceptance and non-digest TOON corruption sensitivity pending. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqR | P2 | fixed | CLI promotion uses the same platform-aware native identity PATH helper. | Existing no-Git CLI promotion case passes; Windows platform path sensitivity pending. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqS | P2 | fixed | Validate artifact boundary before corrupt-byte catch; no-follow bounded read remains unchanged. | R4: moving validation into catch misclassifies the link as checkpoint_artifact_corrupt. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqU | P2 | not valid | Cited injection lands in post-publication reread before executor reread, not after the final executor snapshot. Exact prelaunch message and unchanged peer history pass. | Unchanged publication-to-read test passes all return/execution/launch cases; no claim of an extra reader history certification. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqW | P2 | fixed | New generation reward references use the same artifact identity validation as checkpoint/policy fields; released read parsing stays compatible. | R5: removing reward validation accepts unsafe references; new must-allow legacy and safe digest cases pass. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqY | P2 | fixed | Oracle documentation names frozen 26650e303ec2cb6fcdc6c51092bcc30b2f1ed27c and its required main ancestry. | Documentation checked against controller-compatibility.test.ts:46-49. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqZ | P2 | fixed | Fixture creates missing collection only on SDK NOT_FOUND; native malformed-record failures propagate without replacement attempts. | R9: catch-all yields already-exists instead of item_document_invalid/1. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqb | P2 | fixed | Cooperative refresh publishers serialize with exclusive publication lock and immediate saved-base rereads; equal completed values converge. Ordinary writers are not excluded by this lock. | R10: changing wx to w loses the peer publisher and fails expected evidence_write_conflict/4. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqe | P2 | fixed | Generate, repack and certify in an isolated source copy; publish original documents only after all six acceptances and two fixture replays pass. No rollback. | Failure-after-preparation integration proof pending. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqk | P2 | fixed | Every dataset split uses statePath, matching manifest and write boundaries. | Native dataset regression rejects linked bytes for all four compartments; original split reads pass. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRql | P3 | fixed | Added index.ts to lifecycle feature file scope through pinned pm files, retaining feature text and native history. | pm show confirms all four lifecycle files; tracker-only correction. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqm | P3 | fixed | Invalid-author regression snapshots approval comments as well as SDK item inventory. | Invalid-transaction test now checks audit trail; focused result pending full fixture batch. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqq | P3 | fixed | Describe uppercase process IDs, matching materialized/evaluated state fixtures. | Documentation matches controller oracle source and fixture states. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqs | P3 | fixed | Persist failed acceptance stdout and stderr before rethrowing the original child error. | R11: dropping failure log write leaves old success output and fails exact combined-stream assertion. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqu | P3 | fixed | Pure full-manifest card parsing maps shared schema refusals to card_invalid/4; valid legacy cards still replay. | R6: restoring direct shared parser leaks eval_plan_invalid and fails card contract. |"
  "2026-11-01T07:51:07.368Z",codex-agent,"Local test-selection exception: the existing compose test module probes Docker automatically and started its real fixture cases during the initial focused coverage attempt. This was outside the rules. The module completed its own container cleanup and image-removal after hook; that attempt was then stopped before the later LM Compose module. No broader container or service maintenance was performed. Replacement coverage uses an explicit executable PATH without Docker, so real backend scenarios are visibly skipped and synthetic executable fixtures supply local Compose behavior checks. Partial coverage from the stopped attempt is discarded. The complete corruption-pair matrix was also stopped after verifying three successive native promotions; the unchanged default full matrix remains in CI, with a new focused three-cycle/21-card-replay mode for this fixture correction."
  "2026-11-01T07:58:15.820Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral sensitivity receipts R1-R11 all failed for their intended regression when the corresponding change was reverted in a disposable source copy; every source was restored in finally. Additional R12 reverts the broader runner-publication condition to identity-null-only and fails the real runner-write-failure subcase (retained handle false versus expected true). Fixed cleanup matrix now passes 10/10. The focused successor fixture passes 3 native promotions, 4 receipts, 10 card variants and 21 retained-card replays; legacy padded-parent/environment reads and new strict writes remain distinct. Initial npm run check, explicit lint, build:test, docstring and changelog:check pass. One PM-linked aggregate test hit the default 120-second bound; its bounded 600-second rerun is ongoing. Complete touched-source coverage and final packed acceptances remain pending."
  "2026-11-01T08:12:24.119Z",codex-agent,"The PM-linked focused batch passed 32/32 with the 600-second bound (124 seconds actual, no skips); the earlier 120-second attempt remains recorded as a timeout. Public SDK formatting evidence explains qN: default TOON intentionally omits selection:null and known_regressions:[] that full JSON retains. The acceptance now decodes the whole output and compares with the public SDK printResult TOON projection of the same-command JSON result, using the identical host formatter instead of a handwritten pruning model. A substantive non-digest field corruption must still fail. Fresh preparation and packed compatibility have passed so far; no report, evidence-root or source-digest mismatch has occurred. Original evidence remains unchanged until all certifications finish."
  "2026-11-01T08:14:11.893Z",codex-agent,"R13 (qe and qs) is a real end-to-end failure proof: inject Bun compatibility exit 17 only after successful Node/Bun preparations, final Node compatibility, decision, sequential acceptance and retained-fixture replay. Fixed driver exits nonzero with all three original documents byte-identical and both injected stdout/stderr diagnostics retained. Restoring the previous driver in a disposable source copy exits nonzero after changing original documents and discarding the failed log. Current native packed Node compatibility and decision checks pass under the SDK-defined TOON projection. Synthetic Compose coverage additionally passes 5/5 using a real reference trainer behind an owned fake executable; the first synthetic attempt used an invalid fixture job identity, now corrected to the actual content-bound processJobId. No production change was needed for that test correction. Restored legacy parser checks also cover blank seed parents, padded approvals and padded collection-run identities alongside strict new-write refusals."
  "2026-11-01T08:33:12.930Z",codex-agent,"Additional completed sensitivities: delayed stdout produces all 4,595 bytes of the real SDK decision with the fixed generated probe; restoring process.exit(0) produces zero bytes and invalid JSON (qE). Reverting the Windows identity selector to the Unix tool fails the real filesystem Windows-branch setup (qG/qR). Corrupting a non-digest subject field in actual CLI TOON makes the strengthened decision acceptance fail; the previous digest-only acceptance still passes the same corruption (qN). The README recovery paragraph is also corrected: published runner identities persist, while an unpublished runner requires the original retained ChildProcess handle in the owning controller. This shipped documentation change requires the final archive and its six acceptances/replays to be regenerated once more; the earlier successful archive is intermediate evidence only."
  "2026-11-01T08:53:36.176Z",codex-agent,"P1 cleanup class closure now uses the original SDK failure object as the recovery capability, rather than a registry keyed by diagnostic PID. This prevents PID reuse or copied serialized diagnostics from selecting a later retained child. Unknown/copied capabilities refuse process_stop_failed/4; the original failure can retry the exact native handle, including a false-success kill acknowledgement, and becomes idempotent only after observed native close. Expanded native cleanup matrix passes 11/11, covering unavailable identity, failed runner publication, signal exit and ordinary exit. README describes this capability contract. The earlier restricted-PATH coverage diagnostic resolved Node 24 through its tool link; that link is corrected to explicit Node 26.13.0. Its profiles are diagnostic evidence only, and final scoped coverage will use Node 26 and the final recovery implementation; no mixed-version process coverage is claimed."
  "2026-11-01T10:08:04.189Z",codex-agent,"Additional behavioral coverage now passes for orphan-link and directory cleanup refusals, immutable stop receipts, live LM measured-wall replay, native SDK budget omissions, prefix receipt/artifact/adapter bounds, both Compose executor failures, interrupted-job cleanup and occupied reservation targets. Node 26 focused coverage remains in progress for policy-card.ts; all other changed runtime modules retain their exact tested source bytes. Removed one unreachable policy-card ternary arm: refuse.ts rethrowOperationalRead throws every non-expected error and returns only for PmCliExpectedError, so the following non-expected arm was dead. Real native filesystem programming-error and typed malformed-history regressions cover the reachable outcomes. New sensitivity proofs: R17 accepting copied recovery capabilities fails; R18 accepting a kill acknowledgement without native close fails; R19 reverting dataset split statePath follows a linked split and fails. The current Windows selector revert also fails. All mutations ran only in the disposable proof copy and were restored in finally. Previous cb846815 archive is now an intermediate receipt because of the dead-arm removal; regenerate the final archive after this runtime commit."
