ive status regressions. | Unchanged focused reproduction passes both backend_unavailable and native unavailable cases. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRp_ | P2 | fixed | Restore exact one-promotion assertion together with typed budget_exceeded. | Focused padded-approval budget test passes; assertion restoration is the test fix. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqA | P2 | fixed | Keep strict write refusals and restore legacy padded-parent normalization and environment contamination checks. | Parser and padded-environment tests pass with both read and write contracts. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqD | P2 | fixed | Resolve checkpoint boundary outside missing-byte catch. Missing artifact and valid persisted bytes retain their outcomes. | R3: moving path validation back into catch yields lm_checkpoint_artifact_missing instead of boundary/2. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqE | P2 | fixed | Generated probe branches without process.exit, allowing pipe output to drain naturally. | R14: delayed native stdout drains 4595 bytes; restoring forced exit emits zero bytes and fails JSON parsing. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqG | P2 | fixed | Shared PATH helper finds native identity tools directly; Windows preserves the installed Git-free PowerShell directory and copies node.exe. All five affected acceptance/CLI setups use it. | R15: restoring the Unix selector in Windows setup fails; native lookup, installation-directory and Git-refusal cases pass. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqK | P2 | not valid | The actual SDK harness rethrows errors carrying numeric exitCode. Expected-code cases require that typed exception; handled:false is reserved for untyped released assertions. | Unchanged prospective chronology test passes both fixed/sequential modes and both output modes. SDK testing.d.ts:662-663 documents propagation. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqN | P2 | fixed | Deep-compare all TOON export/replay envelopes with the same-command JSON projected through the public SDK TOON renderer; native omission rules are preserved. | R16: non-digest subject corruption fails the complete-envelope check; the reverted digest-only acceptance passes that corruption. Final acceptance compares 14 envelope pairs per runtime. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqR | P2 | fixed | CLI promotion uses the same platform-aware native identity PATH helper. | R15 and the passing no-Git CLI promotion case certify the shared platform path. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqS | P2 | fixed | Validate artifact boundary before corrupt-byte catch; no-follow bounded read remains unchanged. | R4: moving validation into catch misclassifies the link as checkpoint_artifact_corrupt. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqU | P2 | not valid | Cited injection lands in post-publication reread before executor reread, not after the final executor snapshot. Exact prelaunch message and unchanged peer history pass. | Unchanged publication-to-read test passes all return/execution/launch cases; no claim of an extra reader history certification. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqW | P2 | fixed | New generation reward references use the same artifact identity validation as checkpoint/policy fields; released read parsing stays compatible. | R5: removing reward validation accepts unsafe references; new must-allow legacy and safe digest cases pass. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqY | P2 | fixed | Oracle documentation names frozen 26650e303ec2cb6fcdc6c51092bcc30b2f1ed27c and its required main ancestry. | Documentation checked against the frozen controller-compatibility oracle and source ancestry. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqZ | P2 | fixed | Fixture creates missing collection only on SDK NOT_FOUND; native malformed-record failures propagate without replacement attempts. | R9: catch-all yields already-exists instead of item_document_invalid/1. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqb | P2 | fixed | Cooperative refresh publishers serialize with exclusive publication lock and immediate saved-base rereads; equal completed values converge. Ordinary writers are not excluded by this lock. | R10: changing wx to w loses the peer publisher and fails expected evidence_write_conflict/4. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqe | P2 | fixed | Generate, repack and certify in an isolated source copy; publish original documents only after all six acceptances and two fixture replays pass. No rollback. | R13: real failure after both preparations and final Node replay leaves original documents unchanged; reverted driver changes them and loses failure output. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqk | P2 | fixed | Every dataset split uses statePath, matching manifest and write boundaries. | R19: restoring the released resolve call follows the linked split and fails; original split reads and all four linked compartments are tested. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRql | P3 | fixed | Added index.ts to lifecycle feature file scope through pinned pm files, retaining feature text and native history. | pm show confirms all four lifecycle files; tracker-only correction. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqm | P3 | fixed | Invalid-author regression snapshots approval comments as well as SDK item inventory. | Native invalid-transaction regression passes with approval-comment and complete inventory assertions. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqq | P3 | fixed | Describe uppercase process IDs, matching materialized/evaluated state fixtures. | Documentation matches controller oracle source and fixture states. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqs | P3 | fixed | Persist failed acceptance stdout and stderr before rethrowing the original child error. | R11: dropping failure log write leaves old success output and fails exact combined-stream assertion. |\n| PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRqu | P3 | fixed | Pure full-manifest card parsing maps shared schema refusals to card_invalid/4; valid legacy cards still replay. | R6: restoring direct shared parser leaks eval_plan_invalid and fails card contract. |"
  "2026-11-01T10:16:52.632Z",codex-agent,"Final runtime source is 579c0e7fa0f517f249caed21d1373ca4dfb5caae. Fresh Node and Bun acceptance: evaluation-compatibility, decision-evidence and sequential-evaluation all pass (6/6), plus both retained native-fixture replay certifications (2/2) and 2 native fixture preparations. Source is frozen read-only public commit 26650e303ec2cb6fcdc6c51092bcc30b2f1ed27c: 113 items, 92 done-role items, source digest unchanged. Final archive SHA-256 b64e6759d05e9eab8cca576e731f9716cc54ac83c791e7263779458e36cda98f; 241 shipped files, 180 runtime files. Independent original-worktree build and npm pack are byte-identical to the certified archive. Earlier archive receipts in this append-only history are intermediate. grep for 120e20e in docs and README is empty. PM-linked final regressions pass 62/62 with no skips; check, explicit lint, docstring (58 files/523 declarations), build:test and changelog:check pass; duplicates reports 0 clones. R19 was rerun with the exact released resolve call and its required import: original dataset reads succeed, the linked split is followed, and the expected boundary refusal is missing. An earlier incomplete sensitivity setup was discarded. Final per-file coverage is still being collected, without the two large local policy-card matrices. CI is pending the one batch push; full release verification is delegated to exact-head CI at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/pull/107/checks. No CI success is claimed before that run."
  "2026-11-01T10:28:10.236Z",codex-agent,"Final focused verification: PM-linked batches pass 62/62 + 3/3 LM recovery cases + 2/2 legacy graph cases (67/67, no skips). Fresh policy-card file suite passes 110/110; the two large seeded/recovery matrices were excluded locally and remain unchanged for CI. Additional final-source coverage cohort passes 8/8 plus the last 2/2 graph cases. Native Node 26 profiles certify every changed runtime file at 100% in all four dimensions: checkpoint-artifacts.ts, compose.ts, dataset.ts, lineage.ts, lm.ts, policy-card.ts, process.ts, state-boundary.ts. Totals: 5331/5331 lines, 2343/2343 branches, 401/401 functions, 2269/2269 statements. Aggregation uses Node TestCoverage and the repository computeStatementCoverage algorithm; native reaggregation matches the original LCOV on the seven unchanged runtime files. Every prior-version policy-card profile was discarded; policy-card coverage comes only from the final runtime source. No threshold, ignore or source-scope configuration changed. The earlier broad focused suite passed 476/495 with 19 explicit local exclusions; its unchanged source profiles contribute only to the measured eight-file scope, not a full release-gate claim. The restored exact dataset implementation passes after the R19 revert proof. npm run check, explicit lint, docstring, build:test and changelog:check pass. Full release verification remains exact-head CI after the single push. Remaining blocker is P1 PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRp3, not an accepted deferral. No GitHub thread was replied to or resolved."
  "2026-11-02T05:42:29.465Z",codex-sol,"Resuming the remaining P1 with published SDK 2026.11.2. Pins, typed refusal mapping, command and acquisition regression tests, old-SDK sensitivity proof, documentation and focused gates are in scope. Full release verification remains CI-only; no review-thread replies or resolutions will be made. Auditing the published SDK late-swap behavior because its declarations explicitly retain a stray lock rather than unlinking outside the tracker."
  "2026-11-02T05:54:01.559Z",codex-sol,"SDK adoption now pins 2026.11.2 in package dev/peer dependencies, manifest minimum host, npm lock and Bun lock. README and decision-evidence name the tested host and distinguish acquisition refusal from an atomic no-outside-write guarantee. Raw SDK lock_path_unsafe/4 maps to rl_state_path_invalid/2 through native client calls, ordinary locks, fenceable leases and workspace transactions. The real old-pin negative control temporarily restored both the 2026.10.27 dev/peer pins and its published installed archive: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"SDK acquire.*refuses a symlinked|package .*maps the SDK refusal\" test/sdk-lock-confinement.test.ts failed 5/5 with Missing expected rejection. Restoring 2026.11.2 makes these cases pass. The linked schema-context regression passed 7/7; the earlier none-context invocation was refused by runner configuration before executing tests. Runner result tracking is disabled, so this comment preserves the verified outcome without copying host execution-context paths. The later-open stray-file reproduction keeps the P1 acceptance blocked."
  "2026-11-02T05:56:56.846Z",codex-sol,"Final bounded verification: 20/20 focused tests with state-boundary.ts at 100/100/100/100 (230 lines, 166 branches, 34 functions, 166 statements); exact coverage command is linked on pm-rl-confined-sdk-locks. Final PM-linked regression is 8/8 and the minimum-host activation contract is 1/1. npm run check, lint, docstring, build:test and changelog:check pass. Old SDK 2026.10.27 negative control fails all five acquisition cases as intended and the installed SDK and pins were restored. The new native test reproduces an empty outside lock on a late open substitution with SDK 2026.11.2; the P1 therefore remains blocked rather than receiving an unsupported confinement acceptance. README and decision-evidence now document the shipped refusal guarantee, exit mapping and this remaining limit. No GitHub thread replies, mentions, merge or release."
  "2026-11-02T05:58:57.068Z",codex-sol,"The final PM-linked coverage run in a source snapshot also passes 20/20 and all four 100% thresholds. Child execution metadata records none/snapshot to avoid the inherited tracker-redirection failure; the final runtime source was unchanged. Both item statuses remain blocked on the later-open SDK outside-lock reproduction, and claims are released before the single authorized push. Code and PM histories are committed together. Exact-head full CI is delegated to https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/pull/107/checks and will be linked in the final handoff. No review thread is modified."
